-- #1094 S0 REGRESSION PIN.  An `Effect`-kinded type-ARGUMENT slot is INVARIANT
-- (EFFECTS-SEMANTICS §9, "Index fidelity"): `F <Stdout> a` and `F <> a` are different
-- types, and no direction of the row order `≤` is licensed between them.
--
-- Before the fix `unifyN (TEff _) (TEff _)` routed into the ARROW-row unifier, whose
-- closed~closed arm is a documented silent no-op — so both written rows landed there,
-- the atom sets were never compared, and this file CHECKED CLEAN.  Add
--     unbox : Box e a -> <e> a
--     pureVal : Unit
--     pureVal = unbox quiet
-- and a binding whose scheme carries NO effect row at all performed <Stdout>, on both
-- the interpreter and the compiled binary, with zero diagnostics.
--
-- The mismatch is on the ROW slot only; the value slot was already checked, which is
-- what localised the hole to the `Effect`-kinded index.
data Box (e : Effect) a = MkBox (Unit -> <e> a)

shout : Unit -> <Stdout> Unit
shout u = shout u

loud : Box <Stdout> Unit
loud = MkBox shout

quiet : Box <> Unit
quiet = loud
